{"title":"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Easiest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Easiest)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> both have length 10, sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b6691251a362837413262d094d29f92be951d579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> both have length 17, and the measure of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. What is the length of diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c8d6aaa1d59d7dfca5a5044d41a1565c2ed306.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,0)--(17,0)); draw(rotate(301, (17,0))*(0,0)--(17,0)); picture p; draw(p, (0,0)--(0,10)); draw(p, rotate(115, (0,10))*(0,0)--(0,10)); add(rotate(3)*p);  draw((0,0)--(8.25,14.5), linetype(&quot;8 8&quot;));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (8.25, 14.5), N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (-0.25, 10), W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (17, 0), E);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"212\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9eb223df2c975fc9a4d0cd0b98691c1e4ca178f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13.5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 14\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 15.5\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 17\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 18.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"436\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b230dd623da9b612b75c24f259f6fb5faa8cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD} = \\overline{CD}$\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af840ccac2e6a97aa799681cc6b37a49df8c17f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC = \\angle DCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" />. Angles in a triangle add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18adfe350e554a8902965da703bc60ce56533c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC=60^\\circ$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, the other two angles are also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is an equilateral triangle. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8f5eeb63755700eb790fdc7eddaad29fc49988.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}=\\overline{DA}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"170\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> in half and connect this point to A, dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> in half. This means the base will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296cdeb5dcfdd9d40158b0d039c5d2757e1c04bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and the hypotenuse will be 17. By using the Pythagorean's Theorem, we see that if the base and height are shared, the hypotenuse should be the same. This tells us that the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8bad37c4fa1a9de0f1a384ad643a88b4ffa086ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC} = \\boxed{(D) 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"111\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~Champion1234\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Easiest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Easiest)\">Solution 3 (Easiest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Easiest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Take an equilateral triangle with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is congruent to this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8879abf0d7fbb06bc388aa9ab096a5c37c9bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SAS$\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />, hence it is equilateral. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c2fe7b70baac4980197de81c1090e57efe750c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"59\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=3034\">https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=3034</a>\n</p><p>~pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8\">2005 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 P